A||||12||2M4 Dale||WS6 Suspension Question ???||||5||
Z||000000||2M4 Dale||12-10-2000||09:51 AM||||I have a 85 GT parts car and it has the WS6 code on the build sheet. What all does this comprise of ? The coil srings...the front sway bar...anything else ??? Also will these items , if installed , on my 87 coupe show any real improvement over my "basic" suspension package ? ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||12-10-2000||09:59 AM||||Dale,<P>I think the WS6 package included front and rear springs and heavy duty (larger diameter) front and rear sway bars. I'm not sure if the front shocks and rear struts were any different, but it would make sense if they were more stiff than normal (non WS6).<P>Almost forgot, yes they should fit an '87 (the back will for sure). Front? I think so.<p>[This message has been edited by Indiana_resto_guy (edited 12-10-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||12-10-2000||10:39 AM||||To get more technical,<BR>Springs were changed from 220lbs per inch to 250lbs per inch. <BR>The front sway bar is increased from 7/8" to 1"<BR>14" aluminum wheels and performace tires were added.<P>If I remember correctly all the parts are fully interchangable from 85 to 87.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 12-10-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||rodmcneill||12-10-2000||11:26 AM||||No 84-87 Fiero came stock with a rear swaybar. The 88 GT and Formula did but not the coupe. It might not be a bad idea swapping the springs and front sway bar to your other car. The addition of an aftermarket rear swaybar is money well spent. The GT is supposed to have stiffer shocks and struts also but these I would not change over. Factory struts and shocks even GT models are fairly soft. You will get a better handling car even going with Monroes or Gabriels or if you want something a little stiffer KYBs.||||reg||1
Z||000004||rockcrawl||12-10-2000||12:35 PM||||Apperently there were many more sping options than just ws6 and non-ws6. Check out the listing here <A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/fierov6/OSG/springs.html" TARGET=_blank>http://members.nbci.com/fierov6/OSG/springs.html</A>  <P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||rodmcneill||12-10-2000||01:03 PM||||Thanks Rockcrawl for the spring chart. I see your GT has the stiffest springs. What was the reason for all of these springs? Do they always use the same rate of springs on all four corners? I see your car does. IS this part of the quality control at the factory that the vehicle sits level. If a vehicle was not sitting level would they replace a spring to make it do so?||||reg||1
Z||000006||rodmcneill||12-10-2000||01:12 PM||||On a follow up question does anyone know what the difference would be in poundage between the stiffest WS6 springs and the softest WS6 springs? Also did GM use the same rate for front and rear? IT almost seems that since the Fiero has a rear/mid engine layout that the rears would be a little stiffer than the front.||||reg||5
Z||000007||BAM-BAM||12-10-2000||01:38 PM||||   What is the RPO code for WS6? please tell me it is'nt WS6, I would really feel foolish.<P> Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<BR>Eibach/KYB Susp.<BR>Mr.Mikes 500 series seats,headliner! MOMO Commando Steering Wheel, White Face Race Style Gauges And Soon To Be More!!! YEAH BABY-YEAH||||reg||1
Z||000008||2M4 Dale||12-10-2000||02:33 PM||||Bam...I think that the code is WS6...lol.<P>I wonder how to tell the spring rate from the build sheet though ??? Does it say something else other than WS6 ?<P>I don't need the super stiff suspension. So the factory/low milage WS6 components I have would probably be all the upgrade I need. Just country road stuff not racin' YA Know !!!||||reg||1
Z||000009||2M4 Dale||12-10-2000||03:55 PM||||Thanks Rockcrawl !!!!!!!!! Great chart !!!<P>My GT parts car does have WS6 with 6JH, 7JH, 8YM and 9YM springs.....which according to the chart is the stiffest springs.<P>Guess I'll have to fire up my spring compressor...lol||||reg||1
Z||000010||rockcrawl||12-10-2000||05:01 PM||||I didn't make that list, it's just something I found while trying to identify all the springs I have around. I haven't looked to see what springs are on my 87 GT, but I'd assume they are the firmest ones. It would be nice if each part # had a corresponding spring rate listed. I imagine GM used different springs depending on which engine and trans the car had.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||rockcrawl||12-10-2000||07:29 PM||||All 84-87 Fieros used the same 23mm front swaybar, P/N 10023227. This is the only front bar used on 84-87 Fieros. There was no 1" swaybar and no rear swaybar.<P>My 87 GT automatic has the NYM front springs (second stiffest WS6 spring) and the FJF rear springs (stiffest WS6 spring). There is also no WS6 on the option code list. I assume that WS6 was included with the GT option and therefore not shown.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||bHooper||12-10-2000||08:03 PM||||well, i couldnt resist looking.<P>my 86.5 5 speed GT was the FJF front springs and the NYM rear springs.<P>i wonder why they put the softer springs on the front?  i would have imagined that it would have come with the stiffest springs all around.<P>hoop||||reg||14
